<!--Post: 4048--><!--Time: 1105568684-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4048"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 2:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does any one know if BTK abused his victims post mortum?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4048-->
<!--Post: 4078--><!--Time: 1105648623-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4078"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 12:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very good question.   <BR> <BR>One might think he would LOVE to work in some kind of funeral home? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4078-->
<!--Post: 4082--><!--Time: 1105654636-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4082"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 2:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought the same thing. He likes the smell of death I bet. Necrophilia fits. But not really in the clasic sense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4082-->
<!--Post: 4090--><!--Time: 1105662067-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4090"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 4:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter, <BR> <BR>I guess the essence of your question is: <BR> <BR>&#34;Doe he enjoy the torture/bondage aspect, the kill aspect, or both?&#34; <BR> <BR>Which begs another question: <BR> <BR>If he only enjoyed the torture/bondage aspect, then is he just killing to silence the victims? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4090-->
<!--Post: 4093--><!--Time: 1105664060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4093"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whether BTK abused victims post mortem or not has been vague to me. Some profilers who have written about the case, who had inside looks at the evidence, hinted that he did. <BR> <BR>I think, though, that as sick as it is, you can&#39;t understand BTK&#39;s process until you relate it to the stages of &#34;normal&#34; sex acts. Normal relations involve excitation, the act, the climax. With BTK one could almost relate the Bind to the excitation - anticipation, preparation - the Torture to the process - we all know what that&#39;s like for us, for him, torturing a helpless victim is analogous. It&#39;s the way he revs his motor. The Kill is the climax, and his own writing that&#39;s been released reflects that...&#34;sexual death&#34; in the &#34;Death to Nancy&#34; poem. I feel if any evidence of necrophilic behavior is found in his crimes it will have been minimal, and at best experimental. In a way, Iceteajan, he&#39;s both being practical - for him - and satisfying his innermost need. The torture, in his mind, had to end with the death, or the act wasn&#39;t consummated. <BR> <BR>Ew. Sometimes one has to take a shower to wash off the grossness of just analyzing this guy.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4093-->
<!--Post: 4105--><!--Time: 1105676453-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4105"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 8:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>Sounds like his own twisted form of &#34;crescendo&#34; sex. <BR> <BR>He has to have a control-freak type of personality in order to enjoy humiliating/controlling someone thru bondage. <BR> <BR>Conversely, I&#39;ll bet he could NEVER STOMACH somebody &#40;or anything&#41; having any real control over HIM. <BR> <BR>He strikes me as a guy that can&#39;t tolerate a seat belt; needs to sit on the outside row of a bus or plane for a quick escape, etc.  &#40;A diagnostic MRI machine would just kill him!&#41; <BR> <BR>He is real smug about his crimes &#40;i.e., calling in about his own murder victim in a matter-of-fact tone&#41;; however the guy prolly couldn&#39;t stand any type of domination -- whether machine, person, predicament, etc. <BR> <BR>He is probably a little weasel in everyday life. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4105-->
<!--Post: 4118--><!--Time: 1105697404-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4118"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 2:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well he is not an above average kinda guy thats fo sure. Will pobably be like u said. A weasel.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4118-->
<!--Post: 4123--><!--Time: 1105710154-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4123"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 5:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter, the hanging of Josephine, if done post mortem, may qualify as abuse but as you say, not in a traditional sense. It&#39;s a good question. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4123-->
<!--Post: 4124--><!--Time: 1105710452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4124"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 5:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, I do not believe the hanging of Jospehine <BR>was done post mortem, because I have read in  <BR>numerous  articles that BTK wrote to WPD that he really enjoyed &#34;watching her pleading eyes&#34; as <BR>he hung her up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4124-->
<!--Post: 4125--><!--Time: 1105710945-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4125"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 5:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Curious2, thanks. Due to her smaller size I had wondered if he may have manually strangled her, then hanged her. Thanks again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4125-->
</table></td></tr></table>
